WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.600
When Americans go to the polls to vote for
the president, they’re not actually voting

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.879
for the president.

00:00:10.879 --> 00:00:15.870
Instead, their votes are tallied up, and go
to delegates called “electors,” who supposedly

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.660
cast votes on behalf of the American people.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:24.640
Each state is given a set amount of electoral
votes, based on the number of each state’s

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.150
representatives, plus two for the senators
who represent them in Congress.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.560
Montana has three.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.300
Florida has 29.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.570
California has 55.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.269
And in all but two states – Nebraska and
Maine – the candidate who gets the most

00:00:38.269 --> 00:00:41.470
votes in each state gets all of the electors.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:47.050
So, if a candidate wins the popular vote in
a state like say, Georgia, by only a few thousand

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:50.769
votes, they’ll get all of Georgia’s 16
electoral votes.

00:00:50.769 --> 00:00:57.200
Now, of the entire Electoral College, you
only need 270 electoral votes to win.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.010
This means that candidates can win the popular
vote, but lose the electoral college – and

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.400
therefore the election.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.900
It’s already happened five times.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.920
For a democracy, this sounds kind of…undemocratic,
right?

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.960
Yes.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.370
And make no mistake: it was intended to be
anti-democratic.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.710
Even its defenders accept that.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:23.390
The Founders were mostly merchants, bankers,
slave traders, and wealthy planters.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:28.570
Their goal was to preserve elite rule, and
prevent mass democratic movements – such

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.280
as the abolition of slavery – from taking
hold.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.830
Throughout the history of the U.S., it’s
mostly worked.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.740
For decades, the Electoral College helped
guarantee the dominance of slaveholding elites,

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:45.170
and then afterward of Jim Crow-era planters
in the South.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:50.100
And in the last 20 years, it has allowed candidates
who have lost the popular vote to claim the

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.720
presidency twice.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:56.300
It consistently serves to entrench the rule
of a minority.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:01.060
In some ways, our country is even less democratic
than many of its designers envisioned.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.840
Even James Madison, the chief framer of the
Constitution, wanted a constitutional amendment

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.390
to ban the winner-take-all rules that decide
the Electoral College today.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:15.480
So while the Electoral College’s defenders
CLAIM that it protects against a hypothetical

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.200
“tyranny of the majority, the fact is that
it enshrines something much worse.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.220
A tyranny of the minority.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.410
This happens in two big ways.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:29.690
First, because of how electoral votes are
apportioned, a voter in a small state like

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:34.370
Wyoming or Vermont is weighted heavier than
one in California or Texas.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.460
Your vote just means more there.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.940
Second, because of how polarized presidential
elections typically are, the vast majority

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:46.280
of voters – as much as 75 percent of them
– have basically NO VOICE in the presidential

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.280
race.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.410
If you’re a Republican in a Democratic state
like New York, or a Democrat in a Republican

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.730
state like Mississippi, your vote for president
can feel practically worthless.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:01.360
In fact, unless you live in one of the five
or six states that tend to decide every election,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:07.709
you get no attention at all in a presidential
campaign that’s allegedly supposed to represent

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:08.709
you.

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:13.310
The Electoral College incentivizes most people
not to vote: why should they, when they live

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.540
in a state that doesn’t decide anything?

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.780
The system means that you can safely ignore
the vast majority of the population to focus

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.320
on a few heavily courted voters.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:27.030
And that skews how politicians campaign, as
well as how they govern.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:32.050
Tens of millions of Americans live in cities
facing severe economic and social problems.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.379
But national politicians never talk about
urban policy.

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:40.560
And they rarely talk about the deep poverty
in places like Arkansas or West Virginia.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.190
Instead of the very serious problems facing
our country, which affect both swing states

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:50.410
and safe states, presidential elections tend
to focus on boutique issues that might sway

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.849
a few thousand people in key areas.

00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:57.410
And there’s no evidence that the Electoral
College helps us.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:02.290
Countries like Finland or Portugal elect their
heads of state directly and are more vibrant

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.620
and participatory democracies as a result.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.489
And the Electoral College is just the tip
of the iceberg when it comes to how undemocratic

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:11.629
our system is.

00:04:11.629 --> 00:04:16.739
In 2018, Democrats led Republicans in Senate
races by 12 million votes, yet they still

00:04:16.739 --> 00:04:18.690
managed to lose the chamber.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:23.860
From a grossly unrepresentative Senate to
widespread voter disenfranchisement to the

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:29.330
unshakable grip of elite donor money over
every branch of our government, our entire

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.740
system is designed to serve the people in
power.

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:39.009
It is designed to breed apathy among the working
class while cementing the rule of a few people

00:04:39.009 --> 00:04:42.069
at the very top.

00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:44.839
And the origin of that is the Constitution.

00:04:44.839 --> 00:04:49.809
There is no reason to treat a document written
200 years ago as sacred.

00:04:49.809 --> 00:04:54.169
The Constitution intended to secure elite
rule and prevent democratic movements from

00:04:54.169 --> 00:04:55.169
forming.

00:04:55.169 --> 00:04:59.509
Because of it, every four years we have to
worry about undemocratic elections in a country

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:02.639
ostensibly founded on liberty and equality.

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:05.650
There are simply better ways to run a government.

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:14.560
I’m Bhaskar Sunkara, editor of Jacobin Magazine,
for the Gravel Institute.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.650
Thank you for watching!

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.460
If you enjoyed this video, please consider
becoming a patron of the Institute or making

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.509
a one-time contribution.

